# Mobile: no horizontal scroll

On viewports below `md` (~768px):

- Never force page-level horizontal scrolling to see content.
- Avoid fixed `min-width` wider than the viewport (e.g. `min-w-[34rem]`) on page layouts.
- Prefer `w-full min-w-0 max-w-full`, fluid grids (`grid-cols-7` that shrink), and `truncate` for dense labels.
- `overflow-x-auto` is allowed only inside a clearly bounded widget if absolutely necessary — default is fit-to-width.
- Global guard: `html`/`body` use `overflow-x: clip`.
